           `otel-collector-agent-v2xsb`)\n\n- **Why it breaks the               
           application**\n  - The collector pods start correctly but            
           the **health‑check extension never binds to the port                 
           expected by the probes (13133)**.  \n  - Liveness and                
           readiness probes (`http-get http://:13133/`) therefore               
           fail (`dial tcp …: connection refused`).  \n  - Because              
           the pods are marked *Unready*, the `otel-collector`                  
           Service reports no ready endpoints.  \n  - Down‑stream               
           services (e.g. `product-catalog`, `frontend`) attempt to             
           export telemetry or call other services via the collector            
           and receive **connection‑refused** errors, which cascade             
           into the many “UNAVAILABLE” and “FAILED” messages seen in            
           the frontend logs.\n\n- **Evidence**\n  - **Events** –               
           multiple `Warning  Unhealthy` entries for each collector             
           pod:  \n    ```\n    Readiness probe failed: Get                     
           "http://10.244.162.176:13133/": dial tcp ... connection              
           refused\n    Liveness probe failed: Get                              
           "http://10.244.162.176:13133/": dial tcp ... connection              
           refused\n    ```\n  - **Collector pod logs** –                       
           health‑check extension starts, but no log shows the HTTP             
           server listening on 13133; only the extension start                  
           message appears.  \n  - **Product‑catalog logs** –                   
           exporter cannot reach the collector:  \n    ```\n                    
           exporter export timeout: rpc error: code = Unavailable               
           desc = connection error: dial tcp 10.96.254.140:4317:                
           connect: connection refused\n    ```\n  - **Frontend                 
           logs** – numerous `UNAVAILABLE` errors when calling other            
           services (cart, product‑catalog, email, flagd) that stem             
           from the collector being unavailable and the services                
           failing to complete their request                                    
           pipelines.\n\n**Remediation**\n1. **Update the collector             
           config** (`otel-collector-agent` ConfigMap) to include a             
           health‑check receiver bound to port\u202f13133, e.g.:\n\n            
           ```yaml\n   extensions:\n     health_check:\n                        
           endpoint: "0.0.0.0:13133"\n   service:\n     extensions:             
           [health_check]\n   ```\n\n2. **Or adjust the probes** in             
           the DaemonSet to match the actual health endpoint (if a              
           different port is used).  \n3. Apply the corrected                   
           ConfigMap and roll the DaemonSet (`kubectl rollout                   
           restart daemonset otel-collector-agent -n                            
           astronomy-shop`).  \n4. Verify that the collector pods               
           become Ready (`kubectl get pods -l                                   
           component=agent-collector -n astronomy-shop`) and that               
           the `otel-collector` Service shows ready endpoints.  \n5.            
           Confirm that downstream services no longer log                       
           connection‑refused errors and that traces appear in                  
           Jaeger.'}, 'TTL': 290.12230587005615,                                
